      "id": 1,
      "text": "Esmond Station, once called Papago Station, opened around 1880 as a Southern Pacific rail stop and was the site of the 1903 Esmond Wreck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pima.gov/207/Loop-History?contentId=d72488a4-1cfc-44c4-9f67-2a964f7167b6",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Binghampton Rural Historic District, founded in 1898, was Tucson’s first Mormon agrarian settlement on the floodplain north and south of the Rillito River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pima.gov/207/Loop-History?contentId=d72488a4-1cfc-44c4-9f67-2a964f7167b6",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Lowell Park sits where Pantano Wash meets Tanque Verde Creek, the very spot where the Rillito River begins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pima.gov/207/Loop-History?contentId=d72488a4-1cfc-44c4-9f67-2a964f7167b6",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Rillito Race Track, opened in 1943, pioneered modern Quarter Horse racing and still hosts both Quarter and Thoroughbred races today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pima.gov/207/Loop-History?contentId=d72488a4-1cfc-44c4-9f67-2a964f7167b6",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Arizona Portland Cement, the largest business in Rillito, has operated there since the 1920s and remains a key employer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rillito%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Rillito Vista Community Center, a regional park and recreation hub, anchors the community’s social life in the heart of the CDP.",
